      "text": " B) Zhang is engineer, Wang is director, Zhao is secretary.\n\nWait, but in my earlier reasoning, I thought Engineer is Zhang, Director is Wang, Secretary is Zhao, which is option B.\n\nBut let me double-check.\n\nFrom clue 1: Engineer is shorter than Wang and Zhao.\n\nFrom clue 2: Secretary is shorter than Wang.\n\nFrom clue 3: Zhang and Secretary are not the same height.\n\nIf Engineer is Zhang, then Engineer < Wang and Engineer < Zhao.\n\nSecretary is Zhao, who is shorter than Wang.\n\nZhang is Engineer, so clue 3: Zhang and Secretary (Zhao) are not the same height, which is true because Engineer is Zhang, Secretary is Zhao, and they are different people.\n\nSo, that works.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is option B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is B) Zhang is the engineer, Wang is the director, and Zhao is the secretary.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Clue 1:** Engineer is shorter than both Wang and Zhao. So, Engineer < Wang and Engineer < Zhao.\n2. **Clue 2:** Secretary is shorter than Wang. So, Secretary < Wang.\n3. **Clue 3:** Zhang and Secretary are not the same height. So, if Secretary were Zhang, they'd be the same, which isn't allowed. Thus, Secretary must be Zhao.\n4. Since Secretary is Zhao, from Clue 2, Zhao < Wang.\n5. From Clue 1, Engineer must be the shortest, so Engineer is Zhang (since Clue 3 ensures Zhang \u2260 Secretary).\n6. The remaining role, Director, must be Wang.\n\n**Answer: B**",
