messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nThe words we follow today to talk about ancient Chinese painting are all written by Chinese literati, and because of this, Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time, and they have become accustomed to starting from their own point of view. choose a point of view that is good for literati and artists, and now-- or should have been-- it's time for us to compete with them. And we should also question what they call a good painter or good work. Many excellent non-literati artists do not get due recognition because of the prejudice of literati. Here, we should give them objective evaluation and due status one by one.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of chinese painting theory for a long time\nD) The difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a long history", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the given options (A, B, C, D) is consistent with the original text.Let me read the context carefully first.\n\nThe context talks about how the words we use today to describe ancient Chinese painting are all written by Chinese literati.Because of this, those literati have dominated the discussion space for a long time.They've become so used to starting from their own perspective that it's now or should be the time for others to compete with them.The text also mentions that many excellent non-literati artists aren't getting the recognition they deserve because of the prejudice held by literati.So, the idea is to give these non-literati artists objective evaluation and due status.\n\nNow, looking at the question: which statement is consistent with the original text?.\n\nLet's break down each option:.\n\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level.\nHmm, the text doesn't talk about the appreciation level lagging.It's more about the dominance of literati in the discussion and their influence on how art is perceived.So I don't think A is supported by the text.\n\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice.\nThe text does mention that non-literati artists are getting ignored because of the prejudice of literati.The text clearly states that literati artists have been dominant in the field of Chinese painting theory for a long time, indicating a strong position. So C appears to be a suitable choice based on the information provided.\n\nD) The text discusses the long-standing differences in interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting. This suggests a historical context of diverging interests, which aligns with the text's content.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
