will be pure hydrogen.\n\n2. **Identifying the Underlying Principle:**\n   - The argument's reasoning is that each transition reduces carbon and increases hydrogen. Over time, this trend will continue until carbon is eliminated, leaving only hydrogen.\n\n3. **Analyzing the Options:**\n   - **Option A:** Matches the described principle. It states that if each step decreases one attribute and increases another, the series will terminate with the first attribute eliminated and only the second present.\n   - **Option B, C, D:** Do not align with the described trend or reasoning.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Option A accurately captures the underlying principle of the argument.\n\n**Answer: A**",
