messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nWhether a person is drowsy or refreshed after a meal has something to do with the protein in the food they eat. Most proteins contain an amino acid called tyrosine, which enters the brain to stimulate the formation of dopamine and neo-adrenaline. Birds and fish contain the most tyrosine, but not all foods containing tyrosine excite the brain. Meat contains tyrosine, but fat interferes with its absorption.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following can be inferred from the above description?\n# Options:\nA) Foods with more protein are more conducive to intellectual development\nB) Protein in fish is easy to digest and absorb\nC) Fish are rich in dopamines\nD) There is more fat in meat than in fish', '<think>\nEmpty. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
