messages:   28%|##7       | 165/600 [33:11<05:34,  1.30it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nAt present, there are 3 kinds of GM rice waiting for commercial planting approval, each involving at least 12 foreign patents; 5 kinds of GM rice are in the process of research and development, each involving 10 foreign patents. Some experts believe that rice is the main food crop in China, and if GM rice is allowed to be planted commercially, the state's control over the main food crops may be threatened.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements, if true, would most strongly support the expert's view?\n# Options:\nA) Gm rice has the advantage of resistance to specific pests, but there are few of these pests in rice in china\nB) At present, there is no transgenic rice that can surpass the yield and quality of super rice, hybrid rice and other varieties in china\nC) After the introduction of genetically modified seeds in the united states, the prices of corn, cotton, soybeans and other seeds rose sharply\nD) If gm rice is grown commercially in china, foreign patent holders will prohibit chinese farmers from keeping seeds, forcing them to buy seeds at high prices every sowing season", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option supports the expert's view that GM rice could threaten China's control over main food crops.Let me break this down.\n\nFirst, the context says there are 3 types of GM rice waiting for approval, each with at least 12 foreign patents.Also, 5 types are in R&D with 10 foreign patents each.Experts are concerned that GM rice might make China's control over rice vulnerable.\n\nThe question is asking which statement, if true, would most strongly support the expert's view.So, I need to find an option that shows GM rice could be a problem for China's agricultural control.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) GM rice is better against pests, but China has few of those pests.This seems to support GM rice being beneficial, which would counter the expert's concern.So probably not the answer.\n\nGM rice commercialization will enhance Chinese farmers' access to seeds, leading to lower prices and increased control over the seed supply, which aligns with the expert's perspective.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
