messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn the process of accompanying their children, many parents will encounter the problem of their children lying or concealing the truth. Lying is almost what many parents are most worried about. Their children's bad behavior is even more frightening and angry than their children's poor academic performance.If we say that many parents have not solved the problem of their children lying well, at least most of them should pay attention to it, while the problem of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only worse solved, but also not given enough attention.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is true of the original text?\n# Options:\nA) Parents think that children's failure to report information is more worrying than lying\nB) Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem\nC) Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying\nD) Children's behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents", '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out the answer to this logical reasoning question based on the given context.Let me read through the context again carefully.\n\nThe context talks about parents dealing with their children\'s behavior.It mentions that lying is a problem parents are mostly worried about.It also says that children\'s bad behavior, like lying, is more concerning than poor academic performance.Furthermore, it points out that while many parents haven\'t solved the problem of their children lying well, the issue of children concealing their own situation from parents is even worse and not given enough attention.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A, B, C, or D is true based on the original text.Let me go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: Parents think that children\'s failure to report information is more worrying than lying.Hmm, the context says that lying is more concerning than poor academic performance, but it doesn\'t directly compare failure to report information with lying.It mentions that bad behavior is more concerning than poor academic performance, but I\'m not sure if it\'s comparing failure to report specifically with lying.So I\'m not sure about this one.\n\nOption B: Parents believe that lying is the most unforgivable moral problem.The context does say that lying is the most worried about, which could imply that parents believe it\'s the most unforgivable moral problem.That seems plausible.\n\nOption C: Most parents are more than willing to solve the problem of children lying.The context says that many parents haven\'t solved the problem well, but it doesn\'t mention whether they are willing or not.It just states that it\'s a problem they haven\'t solved well.So I don\'t think we can conclude anything about their willingness from this.\n\nOption D: Children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents.The context explicitly states that this problem is worse and not given enough attention.So this seems to be a direct statement from the text.\n\nNow, I need to determine which of these options is true based on the context.Both B and D seem to be supported by the context.Let me think again.\n\nThe context says that parents are worried about lying, which is more concerning than other issues.So B is about parents\' belief, which is supported.D is about the attention given to concealing, which is also supported.\n\nBut the question is asking which is true of the original text.So both B and D are true statements based on the text.However, the options are A, B, C, D, and I have to choose one.Wait, maybe I misread something.\n\nWait, the context says that parents have not solved the problem of lying well, and the problem of concealing is worse and not given eno