messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nInsurance risk refers to the uncertainty about the outcome of an event under certain circumstances. In probabilistic terms, uncertainty is defined as the probability of the outcome of an event being between zero and one, when the probability of the outcome of an event being zero or one. It means that the event is certain to occur or certain not to occur, and therefore, there is no risk.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is true?\n# Options:\nA) When the probability of an event occurring as a result is zero, the event is determined not to occur.\nB) When the probability of an event occurring as a result is one, it means that the event has occurred.\nC) When the probability of an event occurring as a result is zero , the event must occur.\nD) The probability of the risk must be zero or one.', '<think>\nNothing. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
