t answer is D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D) Xiao Wang is a teacher. Xiao Li is a lawyer. Xiao Zhang is a doctor.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Clue 1:** Z (Xiao Zhang) is older than the teacher. So, Z \u2260 teacher.\n\n2. **Clue 2:** W (Xiao Wang) is not the same age as the doctor. So, W \u2260 doctor.\n\n3. **Clue 3:** The doctor is younger than L (Xiao Li). So, doctor < L.\n\n4. From clue 3, since the doctor is younger than L, L cannot be the doctor. Therefore, L must be either the lawyer or the teacher.\n\n5. From clue 2, W cannot be the doctor, so W must be either the lawyer or the teacher.\n\n6. From clue 1, Z is older than the teacher. Since Z cannot be the teacher (as Z is older than the teacher), Z must be either the lawyer or the doctor.\n\n7. From clue 3, the doctor is younger than L. If Z were the doctor, then L would be older than Z. However, from clue 1, Z is older than the teacher, so Z cannot be the youngest. Therefore, Z must be the doctor, and the teacher must be either W or L.\n\n8. Since W cannot be the doctor (clue 2), W must be the teacher. Therefore, L must be the lawyer.\n\n9. Assigning the professions:\n   - Z (Xiao Zhang) is the doctor.\n   - L (Xiao Li) is the lawyer.\n   - W (Xiao Wang) is the teacher.\n\nThis satisfies all the given clues.\n\n**Answer:** D) Xiao Wang is a teacher. Xiao Li is a lawyer. Xiao Zhang is a doctor.",
