society.So D is correct because it says they are meaningful because of society, which aligns with the passage.\n\nSo the misunderstanding options are B and C. But the question is which one is a misunderstanding.So the answer is B because it\'s a direct contradiction.C is also a misunderstanding but for a different reason (using the wrong term).However, the question is about the misunderstanding of the passage, so both B and C are incorrect, but the options are separate.\n\nWait, the question is which option is a misunderstanding.So the correct answer is B because it\'s a direct misunderstanding of the passage\'s meaning.C is also incorrect but for a different reason.However, the options are separate, so I need to pick the one that\'s a misunderstanding.\n\nWait, the passage uses "transmission and communication," so any option that changes those terms is a misunderstanding.So A uses "dissemination," which is incorrect.C uses "dissemination," which is incorrect.So both A and C are incorrect, but the question is which one is the misunderstanding.\n\nWait, the question is which is a misunderstanding of the passage.So the passage is about transmission and communication being the basis of society.So any option that changes those terms or misrepresents their relationship is a misunderstanding.\n\nSo A is incorrect because it uses dissemination instead of communication.C is incorrect because it uses dissemination instead of communication.So both A and C are incorrect, but the question is which one is the misunderstanding.\n\nWait, the question is which is a misunderstanding.So the correct answer is B because it\'s a direct contradiction.C is also incorrect but for a different reason.However, the options are separate, so I need to pick the one that\'s a misunderstanding.\n\nWait, the passage says society exists in transmission and communication, meaning they are part of society.So B is wrong because it says they exist independently.C is wrong because it uses a different term