n, the argument must assume that the decrease in humidity is the cause of the increase in visits, not other factors. So, the assumption is that the decrease in humidity is the cause, which is D.\n\nAlternatively, the argument is assuming that the time frame is correct, which is C.\n\nBut the question is about the assumption that the argument depends on. The argument is making a causal link, so it's assuming that the decrease in humidity is the cause, not other factors. So, the assumption is that the decrease in humidity is the cause, which is D.\n\nWait, no, D is about the visits being due to illness, which is part of the conclusion. The argument is concluding that the decrease in humidity caused the visits, so it's assuming that the visits are because of the humidity, which is D.\n\nI think I'm going to have to go with D as the correct answer because the argument is assuming that the visits are due to the decreased humidity, not other reasons. So, the assumption is that the visits are because of the humidity, which is D.\n</think>\n\nThe argument concludes that decreased humidity caused an increase in nurse visits by assuming that the decrease in humidity was the cause. This is option D, as it assumes that the visits were due to illness rather than other factors.\n\nAnswer: D",
