messages:   55%|#####5    | 330/600 [52:42<05:56,  1.32s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main content of the given text.Let me read through it again carefully.\n\nThe context talks about writing poems and how it\'s a mutual accommodation between language and emotion.It says that for a beginner, it\'s unpredictable because they might not know their feelings or sentence patterns at first.But once they have a preliminary idea, they can use the book "Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms" to help them.The book provides guidance on choosing suitable words, rhyme schemes, and rhetorical devices to avoid being misled by syntax.It also mentions that if you\'ve read enough ancient poems and have a good sense of language, you can complete your first creation with its help.Importantly, the book doesn\'t teach how to write amazing masterpieces but encourages sincerity to avoid making jokes.\n\nNow, the question is asking which option is the main content of the text.The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nLet me break down each option:.\n\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones.Hmm, the text does mention that the book can help beginners, but it doesn\'t specifically say it\'s because of "rich tones."It talks more about providing guidance on words, rhyme, and devices.So maybe A isn\'t the main point.The creator of poetry does not require abundant emotion or high literary accomplishment. The text emphasizes that having emotion and literary sense is not necessary, especially if they haven\'t read enough ancient poems. So this might not be a key aspect.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
