messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, community banks in some big cities have been closed frequently. At the same time, a series of new banks, such as unmanned banks, 5G banks and smart banks, keep emerging. Bank branches are bidding farewell to cold glass counters and metal benches. The traditional transaction processing functions of bank branches are weakened, and customized services, product experience, social interaction and other functions are increasingly prominent. As a result, some experts predict that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, best supports the expert's view?\n# Options:\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit\nD) Online banking, mobile banking and other emerging, bank outlets as the main channel of service is weakening", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option best supports the expert's view that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.Let me start by understanding the context provided.\n\nThe context says that community banks in big cities are closing often, but new types of banks like unmanned banks, 5G banks, and smart banks are popping up.The traditional functions of bank branches, like cold glass counters and metal benches, are being replaced.Instead, they're offering more customized services, product experiences, social interactions, etc.Experts predict that traditional branches will disappear in 20 years.\n\nSo the expert is arguing that because of these changes, traditional branches won't last.Now, the question is asking which option, if true, would best support this view.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) Customers have to enter to take a number, wait, and deal with simple business, taking a long time.This seems to talk about the process of getting a number and waiting, which might relate to the decline of traditional services, but it's more about the process rather than the disappearance of the branch itself.\n\nThe amateur is suggesting that due to technological advancements and the transition to online/mobile banking, traditional branches will thrive.Option D indicates that these channels are strengthening, which would contradict the amateur's forecast. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
