messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nRight to equality refers to the right of citizens to enjoy their rights equally without any unreasonable differential treatment and require equal protection from the state.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above rights, which of the followings is the violation of right to equality?\n# Options:\nA) In a divorce case, a woman asked for an equal division of the joint property of the husband and wife\nB) Women demand equal pay with men for equal work\nC) A primary school refused to accept students with physical disabilities\nD) A married daughter asked to inherit her father's inheritance with her brother", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option is a violation of the right to equality based on the given context.The context says that the right to equality means citizens enjoy their rights equally without unfair treatment and receive equal protection from the state.\n\nLet me go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: In a divorce case, a woman asked for an equal division of the joint property of the husband and wife.Hmm, this seems fair because both parents usually split property equally.I don't see how this violates equality rights.It's more about fair division, not unequal treatment.\n\nOption B: Women demand equal pay with men for equal work.Oh, this rings a bell.I remember that there's a lot of discussion about gender pay gaps.If women are demanding equal pay for the same work, that's about equal treatment in the workplace.So this doesn't violate the right to equality; in fact, it's a positive step towards equality.\nIn many cultures, inheritance laws can vary.If the daughter is asking to share with her brother, it's about equal sharing of assets.I don't think this is a violation because it's about equal division, not unequal treatment. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
