ncome levels make people more sensitive to price, which would reduce demand, thus supporting the conclusion.\n\nOption C supports the conclusion by noting that many countries already have higher tax rates, making China's 11% rate relatively low.\n\nOption D supports the conclusion by showing that tax increases in other countries reduced private cigarette sales.\n\nTherefore, Option A is the correct answer as it weakens the conclusion.",
