messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nSince the 1950s, the average number of large tornadoes that erupt each year in the world has risen from about 10 to 15. At the same time, human activities have surged, and the global climate has become significantly warmer. According to this, some people believe that climate warming leads to tornado outbreaks increasing in frequency.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, would not weaken the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) There are many types of tornadoes. after global warming, the number of small tornadoes has not changed significantly.\nB) A warm climate is a necessary condition for the formation of tornadoes, and the formation of almost all tornadoes is related to the higher local temperature.\nC) Despite global warming, tornadoes still occur most often in the midwest of the united states, and tornadoes in other regions are rare.\nD) Tornadoes are the product of thunderstorms (that is, local convective weather accompanied by lightning strikes and lightning). as long as strong air convection occurs under thunderstorms, tornadoes are prone to occur.', '<think>\nI am always happy to help.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
