tform and the trunk of a well-preserved tree nearby. It doesn't specify what the platform is used for, so maybe Option A is making an assumption that's not necessarily true.\n\nOn the other hand, the presence of antler ornaments does suggest that there were ceremonial activities, which is part of the point of view.\n\nSo, Option D says that ornaments appear only when ceremonies are held, which supports the presence of ceremonies, which is part of the point of view.\n\nTherefore, the best answer is D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is D.\n\nStep-by-Step Explanation:\n\n1. The context describes a discovery of a wooden hut with associated artifacts, including ornaments of processed antlers, suggesting ceremonial activities.\n2. The question asks which option best supports the point of view that this discovery is significant for early houses and ceremonies.\n3. Option D states that antler ornaments appear only during ceremonies, which directly supports the presence of ceremonial activities, aligning with the context's findings.\n4. Other options either introduce unrelated ideas or make assumptions not supported by the context.\n\nAnswer: D",
