messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nPractice is the sole criterion for testing truth.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to this statement, which of the following statements is incorrect?\n# Options:\nA) Practice can test the truth.\nB) Only practice can test the truth.\nC) There must be other criterion to test the truth.\nD) No other criterion can test the truth.', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I\'m trying to solve this logical reasoning problem.Let me read it carefully.\n\nThe context given is: "Practice is the sole criterion for testing truth.".\n\nThe question is asking which of the statements A, B, C, or D is incorrect based on this context.\n\nFirst, I need to understand what each option is saying.\n\nOption A: "Practice can test the truth."That sounds correct because the context says practice is the sole criterion, so it can test truth.\n\nOption B: "Only practice can test the truth."Hmm, this is similar to the context but phrased differently.The context says practice is the sole criterion, which implies that only practice can test truth.So B seems correct too.\nThe question is asking which statement is correct.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
