blic relations. If G is in public relations, then I and W must be in sales. If G is in sales, then I and W must be split between sales and public relations.\n\n### Evaluating the Options:\n\n**A) G is assigned to the sales department:**\n- Possible. If G is in sales, then I and W can be split between sales and public relations.\n\n**B) H is assigned to the production department:**\n- Possible. H and Y can be in production along with F.\n\n**C) I was assigned to the sales department:**\n- Possible. I can be in sales alongside H and Y.\n\n**D) W was assigned to the public relations department:**\n- **Not Possible.** If W is in public relations, then since H and Y must be together, they would have to be in production. But F is already in production, which would mean production has two people (F and H/Y), leaving only one spot in production. However, production needs three people, so this is not possible.\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe statement that **cannot be true** is:\n\n\\boxed{D}",
