messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nField dependence means that external references are used as the basis for information processing, so it is difficult to get rid of the influence of environmental factors. Their attitude and self-perception are more easily influenced and disturbed by the people around them, especially the authorities, and they are good at observing words and emotions, paying attention to and remembering the social contents in verbal messages.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following belongs to field dependence?\n# Options:\nA) Have the ability to learn independently\nB) Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others\nC) Doing things is dominated by intrinsic motivation\nD) Doing things is dominated by external motivation", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the options A to D belongs to field dependence based on the given definition.Let me start by understanding what field dependence means from the context provided.\n\nThe context says that field dependence refers to people who rely heavily on external references for processing information.This makes it hard for them to ignore environmental factors.Their attitude and self-perception are easily influenced and disturbed by people around them, especially authorities.They're good at observing words and emotions and pay attention to social content in verbal messages.\n\nSo, field dependence is about being influenced by external factors, especially social interactions, and relying on external references.\n\nNow, looking at the options:.\n\nA) Have the ability to learn independently.This seems more about internal motivation and independence, not influenced by external factors.\n\nB) Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others.This could be influenced by others' opinions, which is an external factor, so this might relate to field dependence.\n\nC) Doing things is dominated by intrinsic motivation.Extrinsic motivation is external, so this aligns well with field dependence.\n\nB) Doing things is driven by internal motivation.Internal motivation would mean they rely on internal factors, which is the opposite of field dependence.Field dependence is about not being influenced by internal, but relying on external it.\n\nWait, but the question is asking which option belongs to field dependence.So, field dependence is about not being influenced by external factors, especially social, and not relying on external references.So, option D talks about not having an opinion on others, which is not influenced by others, an internal factor.That fits.\n\nOption B is about being driven by internal motivation, which is more about how they think, not necessarily the actions taken.Field dependence is more about how actions are influenced, not driven by internal factors.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
