thnic conflict, sudden disturbance in public.Terrorism and ethnic conflicts are definitely social disruptions.A sudden disturbance in public would also cause significant social issues.So, this option is likely classified as a major sudden social disruption accident.\n\nOption C: Social unrest, election crisis, coup.Social unrest is directly mentioned in the context as part of major sudden social disruption accidents.An election crisis and a coup are political disruptions, which are also covered under major sudden political crises.Wait, but the question is about social disruption, not political.A coup is not a major sudden social disruption accident; it is more related to political instability than social disruption.However, stadium violence, train station personnel being stranded during spring festival transport, and crowded accidents in tourist attractions during holidays are all examples of major sudden social disruption accidents.Option D includes examples that fit this category, unlike a coup mentioned in option C.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
