messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option refutes the conclusion in the given context.Let me start by understanding the context and the question.\n\nThe context talks about fraudulent text messages, specifically mentioning that X X Group had a prize draw, but even after media exposure, these fake messages keep appearing.The swindlers prefer using shoddy messages because it shows they're too stupid and unprofessional.So the conclusion is that swindlers are unprofessional because they use simple messages.\n\nThe question is asking which option, if true, strongly refutes this conclusion.So I need to find an option that contradicts the idea that using simple messages makes swindlers unprofessional.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it's impossible to deceive others.\nThis suggests that smart swindlers are necessary for deception.If this is true, then using simple messages wouldn't make them unprofessional because they're still smart.This directly contradicts the conclusion, so it's a strong refutation.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nThis talks about police attention, which isn't directly related to the conclusion about being unprofessional because of message simplicity.So this might not strongly refute the conclusion.Swindlers send text messages to attract intelligent individuals who are less likely to be deceived, with the goal of excluding those who are easily fooled. This contradicts the idea that they focus on gullible individuals.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
