messages:   75%|#######4  | 449/600 [1:12:02<03:47,  1.51s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nAvoidance conditioning refers to when a situation of disgust or unhappiness arises, the individual reacts in a way that escapes the situation of disgust or unhappiness. Then the probability of this reaction occurring in similar scenarios later increases.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is not avoidance conditioning?\n# Options:\nA) Detour after seeing the garbage on the road\nB) When you hit something hot, quickly withdraw your hand\nC) Leave temporarily when you feel noisy in the house\nD) Afraid to meet strangers and dare not go to the streets', '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option is not an example of avoidance conditioning based on the given context.Let me start by understanding what avoidance conditioning is.The context says that avoidance conditioning is when a situation of disgust or unhappiness happens, and the person reacts in a way to escape that situation.This reaction then increases the likelihood of happening again in similar situations later.\n\nSo, the key points are: disgust or unhappiness situation, reacting to escape it, and the reaction becomes more likely in the future.\n\nNow, looking at the options:.\n\nA) Detour after seeing the garbage on the road.This sounds like avoiding the situation (seeing garbage) to escape the disgust.So this is avoidance conditioning.\n\nB) When you hit something hot, quickly withdraw your hand.This is a reflex action to avoid getting hurt.The hot object causes discomfort, and withdrawing the hand is the immediate reaction.This is more about fear of pain, not necessarily disgust.All of the options provided are examples of avoidance conditioning.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
