he correct answer is B.\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\nThe argument states that safeguarding personal interests is the only motivation, hence it's the main factor affecting behavior. To weaken this, we need to show that safeguarding personal interests isn't always the main factor. Option B states that sometimes motivation isn't the main factor, which directly weakens the conclusion by showing that safeguarding personal interests isn't necessarily the main factor.\n\nAnswer: B",
