m getting confused. Let me try to structure it.\n\nManager's points:\n\n1. New process reduces sulfur dioxide emissions.\n\n2. New process is more expensive to run because copper must be reheated.\n\n3. Therefore, adopting the new process will cost much but bring no profit.\n\nSupervisor's points:\n\n1. Agree with the conclusion that adopting the new process will cost much but bring no profit.\n\n2. Disagree with the manager's point about the cause of the higher running cost, specifically mentioning that the latest closed furnaces are extremely fuel-efficient.\n\nSo the supervisor is disagreeing with the manager's reasoning about why the new process is more expensive to run, not the conclusion itself.\n\nTherefore, the point of disagreement is about the fuel efficiency of the closed furnaces, which affects the running cost.\n\nSo the correct answer is D) Whether closed furnaces are more fuel-efficient than open furnaces.\n\nWait, but the supervisor is agreeing that the new process is more expensive, but disagreeing with the manager's reasoning about why it's more expensive. So the point of disagreement is about the fuel efficiency, which is option D.\n\nYes, that makes sense. The supervisor is saying that the closed furnaces are more fuel-efficient, which would mean that the running cost isn't as high as the manager thought. Therefore, the manager's reasoning about the higher running cost is incorrect because of the fuel efficiency.\n\nSo the correct answer is D.\n</think>\n\nThe supervisor disagrees with the manager's reasoning about the fuel efficiency of the new furnaces, which affects the running cost. \n\nAnswer: D) Whether closed furnaces are more fuel-efficient than open furnaces.",
