messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nRecently, a number of emotional intelligence education institutions have launched corresponding packages for different age groups. Emotional intelligence classes are popular among parents. Emotional intelligence is the ability to control and manage emotions, and it plays an important role in people's life and work. However, in the hearts of many people, the connotation of emotional intelligence has been alienated. The earliest concept of emotional intelligence is very different from the popular concept of emotional intelligence today. Many people's understanding of emotional intelligence is another way of saying sophistication and flattery. In fact, the core of emotional intelligence is not only the ability to recognize and control one's own emotions, but also the ability to communicate with others and integrate into the collective. The cultivation of these two abilities needs to be practiced in daily life. Whether children can develop good emotional control and social skills depends to a large extent on their parents, and no EQ training can replace the EQ training in daily life.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is most likely to be described next?\n# Options:\nA) Emotional intelligence tutoring should arouse great attention from parents\nB) Parents' practice in family education\nC) Parents should view emotional intelligence training courses rationally\nD) Need to cultivate and improve parents' emotional intelligence", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out the answer to this question based on the given context.Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it properly.\n\nThe context talks about emotional intelligence education institutions launching packages for different age groups.It mentions that emotional intelligence classes are popular among parents.Emotional intelligence is defined as the ability to control and manage emotions, which plays a significant role in people's lives and work.However, the context points out that the connotation of emotional intelligence has become less understood by many people.It says that the original concept was quite different from today's popular understanding, which often equates emotional intelligence with sophistication and flattery.The core of emotional intelligence isn't just about recognizing and controlling one's own emotions but also about communicating with others and integrating into a collective.The context emphasizes that these abilities need to be practiced daily, and it mentions that children's ability to develop good emotional control and social skills largely depends on their parents.It also states that no EQ training can replace the daily life practice of emotional intelligence training.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options A, B, C, or D is most likely to be described next based on the above information.\n\nLet me look at the options:.\n\nA) Emotional intelligence tutoring should arouse great attention from parents.\nB) Parents' practice in family education.\nC) Parents should view emotional intelligence training courses rationally.Not necessary to neglect and worsen parents' emotional intelligence.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
