messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nSome TV ads take the same words, repeated many times in order to deepen the audience's impression, so that the audience remember the product to be promoted. In fact, this is unwise.Surveys show that many long-term such advertising businesses. Lately, they've been in economic trouble, with a huge backlog of products. It can be seen that the business not only did not achieve the desired purpose, but also produced a negative effect.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options best emphasizes the above argument?\n# Options:\nA) Although some tv viewers don't care about the same ad being repeated, many viewers feel it's best to take more of the art of advertising into account\nB) Because the audience is with a good tv program after watching an ad, any ad will make the audience impatient\nC) Although the advertising act does not prohibit the same ad word repeatedly, merchants should consider the diverse feelings of different audiences\nD) Repeated playback of the same ad will cause tv viewers to get bored or even angry, and thus have a strong antipathy to the products that the merchant is trying to promote", '<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option best emphasizes the argument given in the context.Let me start by reading the context carefully.\n\nThe context says that some TV ads repeat the same words many times to create a deeper impression so the audience remembers the product.However, this is considered unwise.Surveys show that these long-term advertising businesses are in economic trouble because they didn\'t achieve their desired purpose and even had a negative effect.\n\nSo the main point is that repeating the same ad words too much is not effective and can be harmful for businesses.They end up in trouble because their ads didn\'t work as intended and might have even hurt their reputation.\n\nNow, looking at the question, it\'s asking which option best emphasizes this argument.The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nLet me go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: "Although some tv viewers don\'t care about the same ad being repeated, many viewers feel it\'s best to take more of the art of advertising into account."Hmm, this talks about viewers not caring about repetition but suggesting that others do.It mentions taking more of the art of advertising into account, which is about creativity.But the context is more about the negative effects of repetition rather than suggesting that creativity is important.So maybe not the best fit.\n\nRepeatedly playing different ads will keep tv viewers entertained and happy, and thus create a strong affinity for the products that the merchant is trying to promote.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
