messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nPeople may be divided into two classes: those who are a little ambitious and those who are not. For ordinary people, a little ambition is a firm motivation to pull them out of their ordinary lives. Without that ambition, can only be powerless and even ignorant, slowly submerged by the ordinary life. In times of change, that bit of ambition can lead to spectacular results.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements constitutes a rebuttal to the above statement?\n# Options:\nA) Liu bei, who made straw sandals, never forgot that he was the emperor's uncle.because of this, he went from empty-handed to one-third of the world.\nB) Although zhang xiong had high ambitions, he was mediocre in intelligence. he worked hard all his life, but nothing was accomplished, and he was bruised and bruised all over.\nC) Liu qin has neither ambition nor special talent, just by virtue of her natural beauty and the help of noble people in her life, she has accomplished many things.\nD) The chrysanthemum elder sister is neither talented nor beautiful, but she thinks highly of herself, constantly toss about, life also lead a prosperous life.", "<think>\n.\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the options A, B, C, or D is a rebuttal to the given statement.Let me start by understanding the context and the question.\n\nThe context talks about people being divided into two classes: those who are a little ambitious and those who aren't.It says that for ordinary people, a little ambition is a motivation to leave their ordinary lives.Without that ambition, they become powerless and even ignorant, slowly submerged by ordinary life.In times of change, that bit of ambition can lead to spectacular results.\n\nSo the main idea is that ambition is important for people to break free from mundane life and achieve success, especially in times of change.\n\nNow, the question is asking which statement is a rebuttal to the above statement.A rebuttal would be an argument that contradicts or challenges the main point.So I need to find an option that either argues against the importance of ambition or suggests that even without ambition, someone can still achieve success.\n\nLet me look at each option:.\n\nOption A: Liu bei, who made straw sandals, never forgot that he was the emperor's uncle.Because of this, he went from empty-handed to one-third of the world.\n\nThis seems to talk about Liu Bei's success.It mentions that he remembered his family's status and used that to achieve something.So it's about using one's background or connections to succeed, which might be seen as a way to achieve success without necessarily having a lot of ambition.But the context emphasizes that a little ambition is needed.So this might be a rebuttal because it suggests that success can come from other factors like connections or background, not just ambition.\n\nOption B: Although Zhang Xiong had high ambitions, he was mediocre in intelligence.He worked hard all his life, but nothing was accomplished, and he was bruised and bruised all over.\n\nThis is talking about Zhang Xiong, who had ambitions but wasn't intelligent.He worked hard but didn't achieve anything.This seems to support the original statement because it shows that without ambition, or perhaps without the right skills, one might not succeed.So this doesn't rebut the original point; it actually aligns with it.\n\nOption C: Liu Qin has neither ambition nor special talent, just by virtue of her natural beauty and the help of noble people in her life, she has accomplished many things.\n\nThis is not about Liu Qin failing despite ambition and special talent, disregarding her beauty and noble connections.This indirectly supports the original statement, which emphasizes that ambition is crucial.So this is not a strong rebuttal as it reinforces that success requires ambition, contradicting the original idea.\n\nOption B: The daisy younger brother is both talented and handsome, but he underestimates himself, rarely ventures out, and struggles to make a living.\n\nThis is about someone who is both talented and handsome but lacks self-confidence and faces financial difficulties.It implies that self-doubt and lack of ambition can hinder success.So this undermines the original concept that ambition is vital because his self-underestimation is holding him back, leading to financial struggles.Thus, this challenges the original statement.\n\nTherefore, reflecting on the original argument, the statement claims that some ambition is essential for success.Options A and C suggest that success is achievable without ambition, contradicting the initial claim.\n\nOption A discusses Liu Bei's utilization of his heritage to prosper, indicating a lack of ambition.Option C explicitly states that Liu Qin achieved success without ambition or skill, depending on her appearance and support from the aristocracy.\n\nBetween A and C, both go against the original idea, but C directly opposes it by clearly stating that she succeeded without ambition or skill.Option A also contradicts the statement but in a more indirect manner by focusing on leveraging one's background, which may not equate to lacking ambition.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]] 99%|#########9| 594/600 [1:21:18<00:07,  1.28s/it]
